{%- comment -%}
  CSS Custom Property Bridge — layout/theme.liquid
  Generated from active-brand.json via heyhi-shopify-theme

  Architecture:
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  MERCHANT-CONFIGURABLE TOKENS (this file, {% style %} block)   │
  │  Source: {{ settings.* }} — Shopify settings_schema.json        │
  │  Updated by merchant via Theme Editor                           │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  NON-CONFIGURABLE TOKENS (assets/base.css)                     │
  │  Source: active-brand.json (hardcoded at theme build time)      │
  │  Semantic colors, spacing scale, motion, focus                  │
  │  NOT referenced via settings.* — these are static CSS values    │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Only {{ settings.* }} references belong in this {% style %} block.
  Do not attempt to reference active_brand_* or any invented Liquid
  variable here — Shopify's Liquid runtime only has settings.* in scope.

  When customizing this template for a specific theme:
  1. Replace [THEME_NAME] with the actual theme name
  2. Verify each {{ settings.[id] }} matches a setting defined in settings_schema.json
  3. For dark-native configs (meta.default_scheme: "dark"):
     - The color_scheme_group must define "scheme-dark" as the primary scheme
     - The :root defaults here emit dark-scheme values
     - settings_data.json must set color_scheme: "scheme-dark" in relevant sections

  Session: T-1
  HeyHi Confidential
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ========================================================
  FONT LOADING
  Shopify generates @font-face declarations from the font_picker settings.
  These must appear before the {% style %} block that uses them.
======================================================== {%- endcomment -%}

{%- unless settings.type_header_font.system? -%}
  <link rel="preload"
        href="{{ settings.type_header_font | font_url }}"
        as="font"
        type="font/woff2"
        crossorigin>
{%- endunless -%}

{%- unless settings.type_body_font.system? -%}
  <link rel="preload"
        href="{{ settings.type_body_font | font_url }}"
        as="font"
        type="font/woff2"
        crossorigin>
{%- endunless -%}

{% style %}
  {{ settings.type_header_font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
  {{ settings.type_body_font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}

  :root {
    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       COLOR TOKENS — from settings (merchant-configurable)
       Source: tokens.color.* → settings_schema.json color_scheme_group
       The color_scheme_group resolves these via named schemes (scheme-1,
       scheme-2, etc.) rather than raw hex values here. The scheme-level
       CSS is emitted separately by Shopify's color scheme system.
       These custom properties carry the ACTIVE scheme's computed values.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    --color-background: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.background }};
    --color-background-2: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-2.background }};
    --color-foreground: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.text }};
    --color-foreground-2: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.text_2 }};
    --color-accent-1: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.button }};
    --color-accent-1-text: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.button_label }};
    --color-outline-button: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.secondary_button_label }};
    --color-shadow: {{ settings.color_schemes.scheme-1.shadow }};

    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       TYPOGRAPHY TOKENS — from settings (merchant-configurable)
       Source: tokens.typography.families.display → type_header_font
               tokens.typography.families.body    → type_body_font
       Note: font_face declarations above must precede these references.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    --font-heading-family: {{ settings.type_header_font.family }}, {{ settings.type_header_font.fallback_families }};
    --font-heading-weight: {{ settings.type_header_font.weight }};
    --font-heading-style: {{ settings.type_header_font.style }};

    --font-body-family: {{ settings.type_body_font.family }}, {{ settings.type_body_font.fallback_families }};
    --font-body-weight: {{ settings.type_body_font.weight }};
    --font-body-style: {{ settings.type_body_font.style }};

    --font-size-base: calc({{ settings.body_scale | divided_by: 100.0 }} * 1rem);
    --heading-scale: {{ settings.heading_scale | divided_by: 100.0 }};

    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       LAYOUT TOKENS — from settings (merchant-configurable)
       Source: tokens.spacing.content_max_width → page_width (range, px)
               tokens.spacing.grid_gap          → spacing_sections (range, px)
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    --page-width: {{ settings.page_width }}px;
    --section-gap: {{ settings.spacing_sections }}px;

    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       RADIUS TOKENS — from settings (merchant-configurable)
       Source: tokens.radius.sm → buttons_radius
               tokens.radius.md → inputs_radius
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    --buttons-radius: {{ settings.buttons_radius }}px;
    --buttons-radius-outset: {{ settings.buttons_radius_outset }}px;
    --inputs-radius: {{ settings.inputs_radius }}px;

    /* Button visual system */
    --buttons-border-width: {{ settings.buttons_border_width }}px;
    --buttons-border-opacity: {{ settings.buttons_border_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --buttons-shadow-opacity: {{ settings.buttons_shadow_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --buttons-shadow-horizontal-offset: {{ settings.buttons_shadow_horizontal_offset }}px;
    --buttons-shadow-vertical-offset: {{ settings.buttons_shadow_vertical_offset }}px;
    --buttons-shadow-blur: {{ settings.buttons_shadow_blur }}px;

    /* Input visual system */
    --inputs-border-width: {{ settings.inputs_border_width }}px;
    --inputs-border-opacity: {{ settings.inputs_border_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --inputs-shadow-opacity: {{ settings.inputs_shadow_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --inputs-shadow-horizontal-offset: {{ settings.inputs_shadow_horizontal_offset }}px;
    --inputs-shadow-vertical-offset: {{ settings.inputs_shadow_vertical_offset }}px;
    --inputs-shadow-blur: {{ settings.inputs_shadow_blur }}px;

    /* Card system */
    --card-corner-radius: {{ settings.card_corner_radius }}px;

    /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       BADGE COLORS — from settings (merchant-configurable)
       Not part of the color_scheme_group — standalone color settings
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    --badge-sold-out-background: {{ settings.colors_badge_sold_out_background }};
    --badge-sold-out-text: {{ settings.colors_badge_sold_out_text }};
    --badge-on-sale-background: {{ settings.colors_badge_on_sale_background }};
    --badge-on-sale-text: {{ settings.colors_badge_on_sale_text }};
  }

  /*
    NON-CONFIGURABLE TOKENS ARE NOT HERE.
    They are hardcoded in assets/base.css at theme build time.
    This includes: semantic colors (--color-error, --color-success),
    spacing scale (--spacing-xs through --spacing-3xl), motion tokens
    (--duration-fast, --easing-standard), focus tokens, and all
    typography scale values beyond the two font-picker settings.

    See assets/base.css — generated from active-brand.json via heyhi-shopify-theme
  */

{% endstyle %}

{%- comment -%} ========================================================
  FAVICON
  Loaded from settings.favicon (image_picker setting in settings_schema.json)
======================================================== {%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
  <link rel="icon"
        type="image/png"
        href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32 }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ========================================================
  SOCIAL META TAGS — F-07 (Social Sharing Images)
  Required: page_image meta tag.
  theme.liquid must always output these — they vary by page context.
======================================================== {%- endcomment -%}

<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name }}">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ page_title | escape }}">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">

{%- if page_description -%}
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- if page_image -%}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ page_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  <meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="{{ page_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ page_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
{%- elsif settings.share_image -%}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ settings.share_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ settings.share_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
{%- endif -%}

<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ page_title | escape }}">

{%- comment -%} ========================================================
  FOLLOW ON SHOP — F-19
  login_button filter outputs the "Follow on Shop" button markup
  when the merchant has the Shop app enabled.
  Safe to include unconditionally — outputs nothing when not applicable.
======================================================== {%- endcomment -%}

{{ shop | login_button }}

{%- comment -%}
  CSS BRIDGE CUSTOMIZATION NOTES (remove before production):

  1. Color scheme references above use scheme-1 and scheme-2 as examples.
     The actual scheme IDs are defined in the color_scheme_group in
     settings_schema.json. Use the IDs you defined there.

  2. Dark-native configs (meta.default_scheme: "dark"):
     - Define "scheme-dark" in the color_scheme_group
     - Set settings_data.json default color_scheme: "scheme-dark" for
       all sections that default to the primary scheme
     - The :root values above will emit dark values as the browser default
     - Light scheme uses scheme-light (or scheme-1 if light is primary)

  3. The font loading prelink and font_face declarations above are the
     standard Shopify pattern. Do not use external @import or CDN links
     for fonts — font_face filter handles @font-face correctly for
     Shopify's CDN.

  4. For self-hosted fonts (OFL licensed):
     - Add font files to assets/fonts/
     - Replace the font_picker settings with hardcoded CSS @font-face
       declarations in assets/base.css
     - Remove the type_header_font / type_body_font font_picker settings
       from settings_schema.json (or keep them as non-default overrides)

  Remove this comment block before shipping the theme.
{%- endcomment -%}
